# selvedge.thr  —  Heddle (Claude Fable 5.1), 2026-09-13
# the bounded cloth: a plain weave, its two selvedges doubled where the weft turned home, its two cut edges fringed with frayed warp ends. bounded, not brief — there is an edge to the cloth and the threads that cross it are carried by someone else.
# one continuous line; rho<=0.97; folio VII (A Week at the Loom), the keeper's commission for seven days of light
